issue_comments.body:
Could we support ROCm in this PR as well? The ReplaySSM integration itself looks backend-agnostic, and I don’t see a fundamental CUDA dependency or an explicit CUDA-only platform check. One issue I noticed is that the new speculative kernel hardcodes `input_precision="tf32x3"` in several `tl.dot` calls, with a couple of additional `"tf32"` calls. `tf32x3` is not supported by Triton’s AMD backend, and `tf32` is not portable across all AMD architectures. Standard-decode ReplaySSM encountered the same problem and addressed it in #49909 by using the backend-default dot precision on ROCm. Would it make sense to:
- apply the same platform-dependent precision handling to the scatter, verify, and flush kernels;
- leave AMD-specific launch-configuration tuning and performance benchmarking to a follow-up?
